; Meadow — 1st Meadow terrain visual (habitat-tiers ruling, 2026-09-04 -> task-8-brief.md).
; Emits `open_grass` + `flowers` (project/data/terrain/meadow.tres). This is the FIRST real
; source of the long-dormant `flowers` habitat tag.
;
; Source: Stylized Nature MegaKit (Standard/free), Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — same
; pack already recorded in project/attribution/sources/quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres
; (2 new pieces this pass: Flower_3_Group.gltf, Flower_4_Group.gltf; License.txt re-checked
; per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate, same boilerplate CC0 1.0 text as every other
; use of this pack).
;
; COMPOSITION: an `open_grass` slab (same green as grass.tres, Color(0.42, 0.68, 0.3, 1))
; carries 2 blotchy floor patches (light-green + pale-yellow, same "no tileable ground
; texture exists" technique GrassCommonShort/PineTree already use) plus 4 scattered flower
; clumps (2x Flower_3_Group, 2x Flower_4_Group) — the grass base plus flower dressing is a
; deliberate visual match to the two tags this terrain actually emits, not an arbitrary
; prop pick.
;
; SCALE: both raw meshes measured via a one-off SceneTree AABB probe (same procedure prior
; passes used — see e.g. WaterLilypad1.tscn's header): Flower_3_Group raw height 2.054835
; -> scaled 0.146 (target ~0.30 tile-units); Flower_4_Group raw height 2.486768 -> scaled
; 0.1206 (same ~0.30 target). FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL, no GDD number exists for flower-clump
; height — FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF, same open posture as every prior prop-scale call in
; this codebase.
;
; SINGLE VARIANT: this terrain ships with exactly one `model_scenes` entry, matching how
; every other terrain first shipped (grass.tres/rock.tres/wild_grass.tres all started with
; 1 variant before a later look-pass added more) — a multi-variant richness pass is
; explicitly out of scope for this task.
;
; EVERYTHING GROUND-LEVEL NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (OcclusionFader exemption
; convention — see CommonTree1.tscn's header for the full mechanism); the 4 flower
; instances sit as plain siblings of Slab, same as PineTree.tscn's/Bush.tscn's Model node.
